@startuml Scenario_2_Brownfield_Project

title Scenario 2: Brownfield Project — Two iTwins\nBridge 9340 Rehabilitation

skinparam backgroundColor white

actor "Project\nDesign Team" as PROJ
participant "ISBM\nProvider" as ISBM
actor "Facility\nAsset Mgmt" as FAC
database "Enterprise\nCIR" as CIR

note over ISBM
  **Facility iTwin (permanent)**
  Federation ID: aaa-111-...
  /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/publication
  /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/request
  /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication

  **Project iTwin (temporary)**
  Federation ID: bbb-222-...
  /mndot/bbb-222-.../engineering/publication
  /mndot/bbb-222-.../construction/publication

  **Enterprise**
  /mndot/enterprise/cir/request
end note

== Phase 1: Project Reads Current As-Built State ==

PROJ -> ISBM: OpenConsumerRequestSession\n  /mndot/aaa-111-.../engineering/request
ISBM --> PROJ: sessionId

PROJ -> ISBM: PostRequest\n  "Send current state of Bridge 9340"

FAC -> ISBM: ReadRequest\n  (provider session on facility engineering/request)
ISBM --> FAC: GetRegistry request

FAC -> ISBM: PostResponse\n  ShowRegistry: current as-built data
ISBM --> FAC: responseId

PROJ -> ISBM: ReadResponse
ISBM --> PROJ: Current as-built (LOC-000001, existing tags)

== Phase 2: Project Publishes Approved Design Changes ==

PROJ -> ISBM: PostPublication\n  channel: /mndot/bbb-222-.../engineering/publication\n  topic: oiie:s5/ccom:ProcessRegistry\n  body: "Replace pump TIC-106 with TIC-107"

ISBM -> FAC: PUT /notifications/...\n  (FAC subscribed to project's engineering channel)
activate FAC

FAC -> ISBM: ReadPublication
ISBM --> FAC: ProcessRegistry: TIC-107 replaces TIC-106

FAC -> CIR: Register via /mndot/enterprise/cir/request\n  TIC-107 (project) ↔ LOC-000001 (facility)
CIR --> FAC: AcknowledgeRegistry (CIRID: CIR-00042)

FAC -> FAC: Update as-built:\n  LOC-000001 now references TIC-107

FAC -> ISBM: PostPublication\n  channel: /mndot/aaa-111-.../asset-config/publication\n  "LOC-000001 updated"
deactivate FAC

note over ISBM: MMS receives asset-config\nupdate via its subscription\n(same as Scenario 1)

== Phase 3: Construction Completes ==

PROJ -> ISBM: PostPublication\n  channel: /mndot/bbb-222-.../construction/publication\n  topic: bentley:construction/as-installed\n  body: "TIC-107 physically installed, field-verified"

ISBM -> FAC: PUT /notifications/...\n  (FAC subscribed to project's construction channel)
FAC -> FAC: Mark LOC-000001\nas field-verified

== Phase 4: Project Closes ==

note over PROJ, FAC
  **Project closure:**
  ✓ Project iTwin channels deleted
  ✓ CIR identity mappings retained permanently
  ✓ Facility iTwin continues operating
  ✓ Next project gets new Federation ID
end note

PROJ -> ISBM: DeleteChannel /mndot/bbb-222-.../engineering/publication
PROJ -> ISBM: DeleteChannel /mndot/bbb-222-.../construction/publication

@enduml
